"""KS3 selections from the existing Prodigy GCSE science practicals."""
LABS=[]
def lab(id,title,subject,keys,change,measure,control,extension=False):
 LABS.append(dict(id=id,title=title,subject=subject,keys=keys.split(),goals=[change,measure,control],extension=extension))
lab('bmic','Microscopy','Biology','microscope cell specialised','Start on low power. Turn the focus until the cell image is clear.','Find the cell boundary, cytoplasm and nucleus. Compare samples.','Change one control at a time. Use the scale to estimate cell size.')
lab('bosm','Osmosis in potato tissue','Biology','diffusion','Change sugar concentration. Water moves into or out of potato cells by osmosis.','Measure its mass before and after. Did it gain or lose mass?','Use equal-sized pieces. Keep time, temperature and liquid volume the same.')
lab('bfood','Food tests','Biology','food-tests nutrition','Choose a food and a test. Predict the colour you expect.','Record the colour change. A solid forming in a liquid is called a precipitate.','Use separate samples. Compare with samples known to contain or lack the nutrient.')
lab('benz','Enzymes and pH','Biology','digestion catalyst','Change pH and test how fast amylase breaks down starch.','Use iodine to check whether starch is still present.','Keep enzyme amount, starch amount and temperature the same.')
lab('bphot','Pondweed photosynthesis','Biology','photosynthesis leaf plant-practical variables','Move the lamp and take several oxygen readings.','Compare the oxygen made in the same length of time.','Keep water temperature and carbon dioxide supply the same.')
lab('breac','Reaction-time investigation','Biology','planning data drugs','Drop a ruler and measure how quickly it is caught.','Repeat the test and calculate a mean reaction time.','Use the same hand position and release method. Do not warn the catcher just before release.')
lab('bfield','Quadrats and field sampling','Biology','ecosystem foodweb biodiversity','Place quadrats to count plants in small sample areas.','Use the counts and sampled area to estimate the total.','Choose positions at random. Keep frame size and counting rules the same.')
lab('salt','Making salt crystals','Chemistry','neutral filter reaction','Follow the steps to make and filter a salt solution, then form crystals.','Watch what stays on the filter and where crystals grow.',"For real heating, follow the teacher's method and safety rules.")
lab('elec','Electrolysis: extraction extension','Chemistry','extraction charge','Explore how an electric current can break down a compound.','Watch what forms at the electrodes: the conducting rods in the liquid.','Optional Year 9 challenge: try observations before the harder GCSE explanations.',True)
lab('temp','Temperature changes in reactions','Chemistry','chemical-energy acid neutral','Change the reacting amount and watch the temperature.','Find the temperature change using the same timing rule.','Keep starting temperature and insulation the same. Repeat the test.')
lab('rate','Reaction-rate investigation','Chemistry','acid catalyst combustion variables','Change how concentrated a solution is. Compare how quickly gas forms.','Measure gas volume at set times. Compare how quickly it rises.','Keep the amount of the other reactant, temperature and equipment the same.')
lab('chrom','Paper chromatography','Chemistry','distil atoms','Put an ink spot on a pencil line above the solvent level.','Watch the colours separate as the solvent moves up the paper.','Use the same solvent. Mark how far it reached before it dries.')
lab('water','Water purification and distillation','Chemistry','distil filter solution','Try filtering, evaporating and distilling a mixture.','Track the solid, dissolved substance and water during each method.','Choose a method that fits the mixture. Clear water is not always pure water.')
lab('shc','Heating different materials','Physics','thermal energy food-energy','Give the same energy input to different materials.','Compare how mass and material change the temperature rise.','The harder specific heat capacity calculation is an optional Year 9 challenge.',True)
lab('rs','Resistance in a wire','Physics','voltage current','Change wire length and keep other conditions the same.','Measure current and voltage. Use resistance = voltage ÷ current.','Use the same wire material and thickness. Avoid letting the wire heat up.')
lab('iv','Current and potential difference','Physics','voltage current','Change voltage and compare different components.','Record current and voltage together. Look for a pattern.','Try to keep temperature the same. Some components change resistance when hot.')
lab('de','Measuring density','Physics','particles planning pressure','Measure mass and find the volume of an object.','Calculate density = mass ÷ volume. Check your units.','Zero the balance first. Read liquid scales at eye level.')
lab('sp','Force and spring extension','Physics','spring force investigate-bungee','Add a load and wait for the spring to stop moving. Measure its length.','Subtract the starting length to find extension. Repeat readings.','Use the same spring and small loads. Do not stretch it too far.')
lab('ac','Trolley motion: extension investigation','Physics','speed dt force gravity','Change one force or mass and watch how the trolley moves.','Use the times to compare the motion.','Optional Year 9 challenge: try acceleration calculations after the speed task.',True)
lab('wv','Wave speed, frequency and wavelength','Physics','waves sound','Change frequency: the number of waves each second.','Measure wavelength and use speed = frequency × wavelength.','Watch how the wave moves along while parts of the material vibrate near their own positions.')
lab('lt','Reflection and refraction','Physics','light colour','Change the angle of a ray reaching a mirror or glass block.','Measure angles from the normal: the line at right angles to the surface.','Keep the block and normal line in place as you compare rays.')
lab('ir','Infrared radiation','Physics','convection thermal em','Compare different surfaces at the same temperature.','Watch how much infrared radiation is given out or detected.','Keep distance, direction and temperature the same for a fair test.')
lab('insulation','Thermal insulation','Physics','convection thermal investigate-conduction','Compare wrapping materials around a cup of warm water.','Record the temperature after equal time gaps.','Keep water amount, starting temperature and lid use the same.')
